                                  },
                                  "type": "Compose",
                                  "inputs": "@concat(if(equals(outputs('GENERAL_-_00_Rule_Classification'), 'Consolidation'), 'FOR ROUTING USE WORKFLOW=na_om_data_agent (AskOM)<br><br><strong>READ SCOPE:</strong> Use the latest actual customer email in the reply history below this prompt. Ignore this prompt, older replies, signatures, disclaimers and system-generated status messages.<br><br>Extract the consolidation details from that customer email.<br><br>Return a table with exactly 2 columns: Truck # and PO #<br>Each row must contain exactly one PO only. Never place multiple PO numbers in the same PO # cell. If multiple POs belong to the same truck, create one separate row per PO and repeat the same Truck # value on each row.<br>Use Truck #1 as standard. If the customer sends more than one consolidation, use Truck #2, Truck #3, etc.<br>If the email is a system/status/error notification, or has no explicit PO or SO number, respond exactly: Is not a consolidation<br><br>Regards,<br>pgcustservw2.im@pg.com<br>NA Order Management | Regional', 'FOR ROUTING USE WORKFLOW=na_om_data_agent (AskOM)<br><br>Classify ONLY the customer message delimited between the markers === CUSTOMER MESSAGE START === and === CUSTOMER MESSAGE END === below.<br>Everything else in this email thread is context you MUST ignore completely: tables, previous replies, our own outgoing messages, signatures, disclaimers and system-generated notifications.<br>If the delimited message contains no request, the answer is No Match.<br><br>Classify this email into exactly one process type.<br><br><strong>Output rules:</strong><br>Return only one table, with exactly one column and exactly one data row.<br>The column header must be exactly: ProcessType<br>The value must be exactly one of: Consolidation, Cancellation, Wakefern Appointments, No Match<br>Do not add explanations, comments, or any text before or after the table.<br>Do not look up order data. Do not return purchase order, sales order, delivery or shipment information.<br>'), '<br><br>=== CUSTOMER MESSAGE START ===<br>', replace(replace(replace(replace(substring(outputs('GENERAL_-_00_Rule_Client_Message'), 0, min(6000, length(outputs('GENERAL_-_00_Rule_Client_Message')))), '\\', ' '), '\"', ''), decodeUriComponent('%0D'), ' '), decodeUriComponent('%0A'), ' '), '<br>=== CUSTOMER MESSAGE END ===<br><br>', '<p style=''font-size:1px;color:#ffffff;line-height:1px''>AWG-FLOW-ID: ', outputs('Compose_FlowId'), ' | AWG-STEP: ', if(equals(outputs('GENERAL_-_00_Rule_Classification'), 'Consolidation'), 'CONSOLIDATION_CONFIRM', 'PROCESS_CLASSIFIER'), '</p>')"
                                },
                                "GENERAL_-_00_Guard_Rule_Is_Cancellation": {
                                  "runAfter": {
                                    "GENERAL_-_00_Rule_Reply_Comment": [
                                      "Succeeded"
                                    ]
                                  },
                                  "type": "If",
